>No sign of the WoY and he still has the book! Grrr.
>	My questions are:
>
>	(1) does the WoY have a consistent escape strategy?

	Yes.  He frequently teleports to the up staircase on the level to
heal.  If you attack him while he is standing on the staircase, he has the
option of running upstairs.  The way to handle this is to wait until he has
teleported away from the stairs, then to go stand on them.

>	(2) given that he doesn't hang around long enough to get thwacked and
>the potion of paralysis strategy doesn't seem to work in 3.1 what strategiies
>are there for gaining the book?

	The most obvious strategy for getting the Book is to _kill him._  I
try to always have some instrument of instant death on hand to use against
him.  Vorpal Blade, the Tsurugi of M., a cockatrice corpse, or a wand of death
are useful in this regard.

>	(3) the Hordes of Yendor trick is a real pain.  Am I going to have to 
>fight an extra 50 or so major league critters per level/plane over and above 
>normal till I ascend, or is theresome way to put a stop to this.

	There isn't a way that I know of to stop it, although you can make it
easier on yourself with either a ring of conflict or a spell of charm monster.
The first gets them to attack each other, the second will tame a great many of
them.  For added fun, have a magic whistle on hand when you charm them.

>	(4) is it true that I need the bell, book, candelabra UNCURSED for
>the ritual?  Given that the WoY curses  my stuff like crazy and that I don't
>seem to be able to remove curse from these items with a simple spell this  
>would make ascension really a matter of pot luck.

	That is indeed true.  A wand of cancellation works well wrt the Bell
and Candelabrum.  I haven't tested it against the Book, so be careful; it will
surely remove the curse, but it might erase the Book.  Potions of holy water
or a _blessed_ scroll of remove curse will do the trick, as will a normal
scroll of remove curse or a spell of same on an item wielded as a weapon.

